{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-01","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"bbe038e9-86ed-5ec6-ab33-316758ddb16d","goalFingerprint":"sha256:8e0ac4d258392a934efea412757ec12bef301175362bc485e28a880598c6e912","pageFingerprint":"sha256:13e88cbcfd98e7e4c3fb3da88221eec20326e18a5c3509863f88c3b6b337e920","currentTitleDe":"Elektronenpaarbindung mit Orbitalüberlappung erklären","currentTitleEn":"Explain covalent bonding using orbital overlap","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann den Zusammenhalt von Atomen in Molekülen im einfachen Elektronenpaarbindungsmodell durch Überlagerung einfach besetzter Orbitale erklären.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can explain the cohesion of atoms in molecules in the simple electron-pair bonding model through the overlap of singly occupied orbitals.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Im einfachen Elektronenpaarmodell entsteht eine bindende gemeinsame Elektronenpaarbesetzung durch geeignete Orbitalüberlappung; Anziehung und Abstoßung bestimmen einen günstigen Abstand.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"In the simple electron-pair model, suitable orbital overlap permits a shared bonding pair; attraction and repulsion determine a favourable separation.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person deutet H2 und HCl mit passenden Valenzelektronen, entgegengesetztem Spin und einem gemeinsamen bindenden Paar und begrenzt die Aussage des Modells.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner interprets H2 and HCl using the appropriate valence electrons, opposite spins and a shared bonding pair, and states the model limits.","transferExpectationDe":"An einer veränderten Überlappungs- oder Abstandszeichnung begründet die lernende Person, weshalb stärkere Annäherung nicht stets stabiler ist und welche Besetzung eine Bindung erklärt.","transferExpectationEn":"Given a changed overlap or separation diagram, the learner explains why closer approach is not always more stable and which occupancy accounts for bonding."},"rationale":"The explicit simple electron-pair model bounds overlap and common bonding pairs correctly. H2/HCl transfer preserves the energy minimum and does not claim that arbitrarily closer nuclei are always more stable. Whole model application remains one coherent assessable skill. No remaining P blocker identified. Current model cases distinguish a shared opposite-spin pair, attraction/repulsion and model limits; coordinate bonding is explicitly a bounded exception.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-02","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"92c99237-1c74-54fc-bf08-9191656afaa6","goalFingerprint":"sha256:39172e4f75403e2596259761b48d10c53b798bd0809d43eab31ef1eefc6772ac","pageFingerprint":"sha256:6d52158395081d77bef63e80118bc255936e5a8a5cc21fe04797a84c2e0e9c30","currentTitleDe":"Moleküldarstellungen situationsgerecht umwandeln","currentTitleEn":"Convert molecular representations appropriately","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann auf Grundlage ausreichender Strukturinformationen verschiedene Formeldarstellungen von Molekülen ineinander überführen und situationsgerecht eine geeignete Darstellung auswählen.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can convert different formula representations of molecules into one another using sufficient structural information and select an appropriate representation for the situation.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Molekülformel, Strukturformel und räumliches Modell enthalten unterschiedlich viel Information; eine Summenformel legt die Verknüpfung bei Isomeren nicht eindeutig fest.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Molecular formula, structural formula and spatial model provide different information; an isomeric molecular formula does not uniquely determine connectivity.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person überführt ausreichend bestimmte Ethanol- oder Ethen-Darstellungen konsistent ineinander und prüft Atome, Bindigkeiten und vorhandene freie Elektronenpaare.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner consistently converts sufficiently specified ethanol or ethene representations and checks atoms, valence and represented lone pairs.","transferExpectationDe":"Für C2H6O unterscheidet die lernende Person Ethanol und Dimethylether und benennt die zusätzliche Strukturinformation, die zur eindeutigen Umwandlung benötigt wird.","transferExpectationEn":"For C2H6O the learner distinguishes ethanol from dimethyl ether and identifies the extra structural information needed for a unique conversion."},"rationale":"Conversion among molecular representations is scientifically assessable when sufficient structure information is supplied. The new condition prevents an impossible unique inverse from molecular formula alone; the ethanol/dimethyl-ether C2H6O comparison makes nonuniqueness concrete. No remaining P blocker identified. Current whole structure cases give the information needed for ethene and ethanol conversions, valence and full electron-pair checks and a fresh same-formula isomer distinction.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-03","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"c0f1bf09-5a70-5006-b1e9-e91f786a63bf","goalFingerprint":"sha256:5f87b6ab5f6421d137d2ae244f112a6a01179b3387a0fa962b0bfd56bf0ee65e","pageFingerprint":"sha256:8a8282934327af68f57088e41278d21dea8a9fdf9525aeff7778e589347c62d9","currentTitleDe":"Stoffkreisläufe mit Reaktionen und physikalischen Vorgängen beschreiben","currentTitleEn":"Describe matter cycles using reactions and physical processes","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann verschiedene Typen chemischer Reaktionen und physikalischer Vorgänge nutzen, um Stoffkreisläufe in Natur und Technik fachlich zu beschreiben.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can use different types of chemical reactions and physical processes to describe matter cycles in nature and technology.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Stoffkreisläufe verbinden Stofftransport, physikalische Zustandsänderungen und chemische Umwandlungen unter Atomerhaltung; ein Stoffkreislauf ist kein geschlossener Energiekreislauf.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Material cycles connect transport, physical state changes and chemical transformations while conserving atoms; a material cycle is not a closed energy cycle.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person erklärt ausgewählte Kohlenstoff- und Kalkkreislaufschritte mit passenden Teilchen oder Reaktionsgleichungen und unterscheidet Reaktion von Transport oder Phasenwechsel.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner explains selected carbon and lime cycle steps using appropriate particles or equations and distinguishes reaction from transport or phase change.","transferExpectationDe":"In einer veränderten Kreislaufdarstellung ordnet die lernende Person etwa CO2-Aufnahme, Carbonatbildung und Verdunstung begründet ein und verfolgt Stoff und Energie getrennt.","transferExpectationEn":"In a changed cycle diagram the learner justifies the classification of CO2 uptake, carbonate formation and evaporation, tracking matter and energy separately."},"rationale":"The goal coherently relates carbon and lime cycles to material transformations and conservation. It need not equate material cycling with energy cycling. Current physical CO2 transport and molecular transformations are differentiated. No remaining P blocker identified. Calcium carbonate burning/hydration/carbonation equations conserve atoms; the fresh cycle reasoning distinguishes chemical reaction from phase/transport and energy input from material conservation. Actual corrected image separates invisible vapour, liquid droplets and precipitation.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-04","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"f85b4651-50ea-5b42-b193-3465c05257a7","goalFingerprint":"sha256:9ffb4363e6e864a302afd1ae4ae743606b402cdde234375ccc281b9043c34ac8","pageFingerprint":"sha256:b96c82a7a35d2978ed34515588bc1fad582b61e3cb74bb49f4fe9bb80ab8d660","currentTitleDe":"Molekülorbital-Modelle anwenden","currentTitleEn":"Apply molecular orbital models","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann einfache MO-Diagramme (z. B. O2, N2) interpretieren und Bindungsordnung ableiten.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can interpret simple MO diagrams (e.g. O2, N2) and derive bond order.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"In einem vorgegebenen Valenz-MO-Schema ergibt die halbe Differenz bindender und antibindender Elektronenzahlen die Bindungsordnung; ungepaarte Elektronen erlauben eine begrenzte Aussage zum Magnetismus.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"In a supplied valence MO scheme, half the difference between bonding and antibonding electron counts gives bond order; unpaired electrons support a bounded magnetic interpretation.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person liest die tatsächlichen Besetzungen eines N2- oder O2-Schemas, zählt selbst und begründet Bindungsordnung und gegebenenfalls ungepaarte Elektronen.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner reads the actual N2 or O2 orbital occupancies, independently counts electrons and justifies bond order and, where applicable, unpaired electrons.","transferExpectationDe":"Beim Übergang zu N2+ oder O2+ bestimmt die lernende Person aus dem jeweils höchsten besetzten Orbital die geänderte Besetzung und erklärt den unterschiedlichen Einfluss auf die Bindungsordnung.","transferExpectationEn":"For N2+ or O2+, the learner determines the changed occupancy from the highest occupied orbital and explains its different effect on bond order."},"rationale":"Interpret supplied simple MO diagrams and derive bond order is accurate and coherent at the stated LK scope. It requires diagram reading and justified electron counts, not deriving a full quantitative MO energy model or performing an experiment. Scientific MO substance is sound: N2 valence counts 8 bonding/2 antibonding yield 3; removing highest occupied bonding sigma2p for N2+ yields 2.5. O2 8/4 yields 2, two singly occupied pi-star orbitals account for paramagnetism; O2+ loses an antibonding electron and yields 2.5. Both whole cases nevertheless have a false retained practical-execution obligation. P remains REVISE; this D KEEP does not close it.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"revise","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-05","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"91cd4728-b811-562a-970b-18b81dfb4bdf","goalFingerprint":"sha256:a13ea12c7c844f97972eca0447b82a6c7a63503e1afd8fc262ea6d1fcc6c2280","pageFingerprint":"sha256:785e9ac001aaf30618359a14437ecb4cc3d854d30d542f1c4cb0ada5392b5277","currentTitleDe":"Polare Eigenschaften erklären","currentTitleEn":"Explain polar properties","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann Dipol-Dipol-Wechselwirkungen und Wasserstoffbrücken zur Deutung von Löslichkeit und Siedetemperatur heranziehen.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can use dipole-dipole interactions and hydrogen bonds to interpret solubility and boiling temperature.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"London-Kräfte wirken zwischen allen Molekülen; permanente Dipole und geeignete Wasserstoffbrücken verändern zusätzlich intermolekulare Anziehung und damit Stoffeigenschaften.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"London forces act between all molecules; permanent dipoles and suitable hydrogen bonds add intermolecular attraction and affect properties.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person vergleicht Propan, Dimethylether und Ethanol anhand vorgegebener Strukturen und Siededaten, trennt molare Masse von Wechselwirkungen und erklärt Wasserstoffbrückendonator und -akzeptor.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner compares propane, dimethyl ether and ethanol using supplied structures and boiling data, separates molar mass from interactions and explains hydrogen-bond donation and acceptance.","transferExpectationDe":"Für einen Ether in Wasser begründet die lernende Person dessen Akzeptorrolle trotz fehlender OH-Gruppe und grenzt eine qualitative Löslichkeitsdeutung von einer unbelegten vollständigen Mischbarkeitsaussage ab.","transferExpectationEn":"For an ether in water, the learner explains its acceptor role despite having no OH group and distinguishes qualitative solubility reasoning from an unsupported complete-miscibility claim."},"rationale":"Interpreting solubility and boiling behaviour using permanent dipoles and hydrogen bonds is a coherent structure-property competence. The current context also retains London forces and appropriate limits on qualitative comparisons. No remaining P blocker identified. The added propane/dimethyl ether/ethanol comparison separates comparable masses, permanent dipole-dipole interaction and a hydrogen-bond donor; ether can accept hydrogen bonds from water without possessing an OH group. No unsupported complete miscibility or quantitative boiling prediction is required.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-06","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"cf270aaf-235a-55a7-94a2-c4d9d7570a6b","goalFingerprint":"sha256:b07469051202ac5c1e72159576aeb32ae3ae02bce1684938dccd0bb0fc22bde1","pageFingerprint":"sha256:fffe56278cd142ca8566e9e29d21f1cd0c50ca2ff2d9c63647b4efd3b812de38","currentTitleDe":"Proteine mit der Biuret-Reaktion nachweisen und erklären","currentTitleEn":"Detect and explain proteins using the biuret assay","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann kontrollierte Biuret-Nachweise durchführen, positive und negative Befunde auswerten und die violette Färbung als Koordination von Kupfer(II)-Ionen durch geeignete Peptidgruppen erklären.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can carry out controlled biuret assays, evaluate positive and negative results and explain the violet colour through copper(II) coordination by suitable peptide groups.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Die violette Biuretreaktion beruht im geeigneten alkalischen Milieu auf Cu(II)-Koordination durch geeignete Peptidgruppen; blaue Lösungen oder Trübungen sind kein gleichwertiger positiver Befund.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"The violet Biuret response involves Cu(II) coordination by suitable peptide groups under appropriate alkaline conditions; blue solutions or precipitates are not equivalent positive results.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person führt die genehmigte kontrollierte Untersuchung tatsächlich durch, dokumentiert reale Beobachtungen bei festgehaltenen Bedingungen, prüft Positiv- und Blindkontrolle und erklärt den Befund im Teilchenmodell.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner actually carries out the authorized controlled investigation, records real observations under fixed conditions, checks positive and blank controls and explains the result with a particle model.","transferExpectationDe":"Bei verändertem Proteinanteil oder ungültiger Kontrolle entscheidet die lernende Person begründet über Aussagegrenzen, Ursachenprüfung und erforderliche neue Messung, ohne fremde Daten als eigene Durchführung auszugeben.","transferExpectationEn":"For a changed protein content or invalid control, the learner justifies inference limits, checks causes and determines whether a new measurement is needed without presenting supplied data as personal execution."},"rationale":"The description explicitly requires actually performing a controlled Biuret investigation, evaluating positive and negative controls and explaining violet Cu(II) coordination to suitable peptide groups. These are connected aspects of one experiment competence. No remaining P blocker identified. The complete bilingual SOP supplies teacher-authorized local risk assessment, measured quantities, fixed prevalidated CuSO4 dose, matched controls, real timed observations and cause-based repeat/postponement. Predictions or supplied reports do not prove actual performance. Blue free-amino-acid complexes and Cu(OH)2 precipitation are not violet peptide positives; Cu remains +II and disposal is local heavy-metal disposal, not a learner acidification recipe.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-07","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"b8d3b453-d638-5518-aab0-d84ec2e8567c","goalFingerprint":"sha256:7cfe6610ec81b9510eebe1a403f40740cdb6cf50176512a16397f87b103a6358","pageFingerprint":"sha256:e90385b4224bb27bf39d21e2b1c8199d3f4bc6c28a35de1ed071326170b2e24a","currentTitleDe":"Reaktivität aromatischer Systeme begründen","currentTitleEn":"Explain aromatic reactivity","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann die Reaktivität aromatischer Systeme anhand ihrer Elektronendelokalisierung begründen.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can explain the reactivity of aromatic systems in terms of their electron delocalization.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Delokalisierung stabilisiert das aromatische System; eine elektrophile Substitution verliert die Aromatizität vorübergehend und stellt sie durch Protonenabgabe wieder her.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Delocalization stabilizes the aromatic system; electrophilic substitution temporarily loses aromaticity and restores it through proton loss.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person verfolgt Elektronenverteilung, Ladung und Bindungen eines vorgegebenen sigma-Komplexes und begründet die Rückbildung des aromatischen Systems statt einer pauschalen Reaktionsträgheit.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner tracks electron distribution, charge and bonds in a supplied sigma complex and explains restoration of aromaticity rather than claiming blanket inertness.","transferExpectationDe":"An einem neuen NO2+-Papierfall vergleicht die lernende Person Protonenabgabe und eine ausdrücklich hypothetische Abfangreaktion und erklärt anhand einer gegebenen Hydrierung, weshalb aromatisch nicht niemals Addition bedeutet.","transferExpectationEn":"In a fresh NO2+ paper case, the learner compares proton loss with an explicitly hypothetical capture step and uses supplied hydrogenation to explain why aromatic does not mean addition is impossible."},"rationale":"Explaining aromatic reactivity through delocalization is coherent. Temporary loss of aromaticity in a sigma complex and restoration by proton loss justify substitution under stated conditions without claiming that aromatics never undergo addition. The supplied NO2+ sigma-complex paper case is chemically balanced: H+ elimination restores aromatic C6H5NO2, while explicitly hypothetical chloride capture leaves a nonaromatic neutral adduct. Hydrogenation C6H6 + 3 H2 to C6H12 is a bounded counterexample. The case nevertheless adds an unjustified practical-execution obligation despite calling itself a paper case. P remains REVISE; this D KEEP does not close it.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"revise","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-08","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"28c90c6a-3020-5c51-ac40-d802f3f12d2d","goalFingerprint":"sha256:5e7666abb7cd2c4c761356fcd30cccad0080ed13ebcaeb84fb8683e8b420f9c5","pageFingerprint":"sha256:0399469ef7f04b02d002e2757abc3011972474268bd53991ea3ad0290d7d06b7","currentTitleDe":"Titrationskurven datengestützt deuten","currentTitleEn":"Interpret titration curves using data","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann aus bereitgestellten Titrationsdaten den Verlauf einer Titrationskurve, den Äquivalenzbereich und vorhandene Halbäquivalenz- oder Pufferbereiche erkennen, mit den jeweils pH-bestimmenden Teilchen erklären und daraus begrenzte Aussagen zu Stoffklasse und geeigneten Indikatoren ableiten.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can use supplied titration data to identify curve behaviour, the equivalence region and any half-equivalence or buffer regions, explain them using the pH-controlling species, and derive bounded conclusions about substance class and suitable indicators.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Titrationskurven verknüpfen Stoffmengenverhältnis und Säure-Base-Gleichgewichte mit Anfangs-, Puffer-, Äquivalenz- und Überschussbereichen; Neutralität und Äquivalenz sind verschiedene Begriffe.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Titration curves connect mole ratios and acid-base equilibria with initial, buffer, equivalence and excess regions; neutrality and equivalence are distinct concepts.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person deutet vorgegebene starke und schwache Säure- oder Basenkurven, lokalisiert charakteristische Bereiche und begründet einen passenden Indikator aus dem tatsächlichen steilen Bereich.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner interprets supplied strong and weak acid or base curves, locates characteristic regions and justifies an indicator using the actual steep interval.","transferExpectationDe":"Bei einer umgekehrten Titrationsrichtung, verändertem pKw oder einer mehrstufigen Glycinkurve begründet die lernende Person die veränderte qualitative Deutung, ohne Äquivalenz stets mit pH 7 oder einem beliebigen Zwischenpunkt mit guter Pufferung gleichzusetzen.","transferExpectationEn":"For reversed titration direction, changed pKw or a multistage glycine curve, the learner explains the changed qualitative interpretation without equating equivalence with pH 7 or any intermediate point with effective buffering."},"rationale":"Reading and interpreting titration curves coherently links characteristic curve regions, equivalence and neutral conditions, buffering and indicator choice. It does not add an obligatory numerical pH-calculation competence simply because supporting cases provide computed data. No remaining P blocker identified after reading all five whole current materials. Strong-acid and weak-acid tables, sharp endpoint neighbourhood and pKw-dependent neutral pH are consistent. Base cases distinguish strong and weak bases with different equivalence pH; the synthetic glycine two-stage table does not treat its first ampholyte point as a strong buffer. The actual image differentiates acid dissociation, acetate hydrolysis and OH excess. Case-specific calculation routes remain conditional, not a new universal quota.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-09","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"e20d205f-03a4-5f96-b456-9b20460605a2","goalFingerprint":"sha256:9ff3425b376074e63ed2149a0ca9c8b837aaf8b1c2582e37f10d9d57b6f7bf7e","pageFingerprint":"sha256:d77c9de3a9b206df537a85b92e230e58dcda58fb45b59454dafe672ef45e46d2","currentTitleDe":"Life-Cycle-Assessment anwenden","currentTitleEn":"Apply Life Cycle Assessment","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann vereinfachte Ökobilanzen für Energieträger erstellen und interpretieren.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can create and interpret simplified life cycle assessments for energy carriers.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Umweltbilanzen sind nur bei gleicher Funktion, konsistenten Systemgrenzen und offengelegten Annahmen vergleichbar; eine einzelne Klimakategorie ersetzt keine vollständige Umweltbewertung.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Environmental balances are comparable only with a common function, consistent system boundaries and explicit assumptions; a climate category alone is not a complete environmental assessment.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person normalisiert vorgegebene Daten auf dieselbe Nutzfunktion, begründet berücksichtigte Beiträge und Gutschriften und trennt Daten, Unsicherheit und Bewertungskriterien.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner normalizes supplied data to the same useful function, justifies included contributions and credits and separates data, uncertainty and evaluation criteria.","transferExpectationDe":"Bei verändertem Wirkungsgrad oder tatsächlich genutzter statt nur angebotener Wärme prüft die lernende Person, ob eine Rangfolge oder Gutschrift noch gilt, und begrenzt das Ergebnis auf die erfassten Wirkungskategorien.","transferExpectationEn":"For changed efficiency or actually used rather than merely available heat, the learner tests whether a ranking or credit still applies and limits the conclusion to the assessed impact categories."},"rationale":"Comparing environmental balances using a consistent function, boundary and justified weighting is accurate and assessable; the current cases explicitly bound climate-only inventories and do not claim a complete environmental ranking. No remaining P blocker identified. Equal wheel-work normalization changes 40/120 g inventory values by the given 1.2 input factor to 48/144 versus 95, preserving function. Hydrogen heat credits use only actual substituted heat, with gross-minus-credit arithmetic and no double transport credit. The actual corrected graphic has consistent legend, stacked categories and common electricity function; it is illustrative rather than measured inventory data.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-10","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"7dc80ee2-64e3-50c1-8aaa-0fef0ed0919d","goalFingerprint":"sha256:9097ae929906c69d4477b16f6718eb40f4947ee21d7a64728215726d8bb55610","pageFingerprint":"sha256:efd6926dd8b0cabe25118b6dd66acbf0ac10a3d7c1c46f8f9506096e52cb5e37","currentTitleDe":"Künstliche Photosynthese und Wasserstoffspeicherung bewerten","currentTitleEn":"Evaluate artificial photosynthesis and hydrogen storage","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann elektrochemische und photokatalytische Wasserspaltung sowie physikalische und chemische Wasserstoffspeicherung vergleichen und im Hinblick auf künstliche Photosynthese, Rohstoff- und Katalysatorbedarf sowie Energiespeicherpotenzial ökonomisch und ökologisch bewerten.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can compare electrochemical and photocatalytic water splitting as well as physical and chemical hydrogen storage and evaluate them economically and ecologically with respect to artificial photosynthesis, raw materials, catalysts, and energy storage potential.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Wasserstoff ist ein Energieträger; Herstellung, Speicherung und Rückumwandlung haben eigene Stoff-, Energie- und Systemgrenzen, deren Verluste sich entlang einer Kette auswirken.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Hydrogen is an energy carrier; production, storage and reconversion have distinct material, energy and system boundaries, with losses acting along the chain.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person erklärt vorgegebene Herstellungspfade mit ausgeglichener Wasserspaltung, verfolgt Wirkungsgrade und vergleicht Speichermassen unter Einbeziehung des gesamten Speichersystems.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner explains supplied production routes with balanced water splitting, follows efficiencies and compares storage masses using the entire storage system.","transferExpectationDe":"Bei einem geänderten Sonnenenergiepfad oder Speichersystem bewertet die lernende Person nutzbare Energie auf gemeinsamer Basis und behandelt zusätzlich benötigte Wärme getrennt von elektrischem Ertrag.","transferExpectationEn":"For a changed solar-energy route or storage system, the learner evaluates usable energy on a common basis and treats additional heat separately from electrical yield."},"rationale":"Discussing hydrogen pathways, storage and energy conversion is a connected system competence. Balanced water splitting, efficiency boundaries and storage-system mass distinguish mechanism from usable delivered energy. No remaining P blocker identified. The stated solar-to-hydrogen paths give 1.19 and 0.68 from the 10-unit input; storage examples distinguish 1/11 and 2/100 hydrogen mass fractions, and heat is kept separate from electric output. The actual corrected image has cathode negative/anode positive, correct water-splitting stoichiometry, no triatomic hydrogen clusters, and atomic hydrogen in the hydride illustration.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-11","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"a78aacf9-92ea-5627-8776-a595111f754c","goalFingerprint":"sha256:1f428866a73241ec752ce8b83c3ed0ee98c16498b5883219aa9a74df34f626cd","pageFingerprint":"sha256:93a843e0688a72f6881bede3aad8213951e171b82f90d580de0da5748e1cd2d6","currentTitleDe":"Zusammensetzung moderner Waschmittel","currentTitleEn":"Composition of modern detergents","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann Funktionen von Wasserenthärtern (Buildern), Bleichsystemen, Enzymen und Hilfsstoffen erklären.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can explain the functions of water softeners (builders), bleaching systems, enzymes and auxiliaries.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Waschmittelbestandteile erfüllen verschiedene Funktionen: Tenside unterstützen Schmutzentfernung, Builder binden Härteionen, Enzyme katalysieren geeignete Hydrolysen, Bleichmittel oxidieren und Aufheller fluoreszieren.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Detergent components serve different functions: surfactants aid soil removal, builders bind hardness ions, enzymes catalyse suitable hydrolyses, bleaches oxidize and brighteners fluoresce.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person ordnet begründet Komponenten eines vorgegebenen Waschmittels passenden Flecken, Wasserbedingungen und Textilien zu und erklärt die jeweils zugrunde liegende Wirkung.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner justifies matching components of a supplied detergent to stains, water conditions and fabrics and explains the underlying effects.","transferExpectationDe":"Bei härterem Wasser, einem Proteintextil oder veränderter Bleichverträglichkeit begründet die lernende Person eine angepasste Wahl und verwechselt optische Aufhellung nicht mit zusätzlichem Abbau von Schmutz.","transferExpectationEn":"For harder water, a protein textile or changed bleach tolerance, the learner justifies an adapted choice and does not confuse optical brightening with additional soil degradation."},"rationale":"The explicit water-softener/builders term clarifies a functional detergent component without expanding the goal into an independent recall catalogue. Explaining interacting washing components and suitable conditions remains one coherent model-based competence. No remaining P blocker identified. Whole cases distinguish hardness-binding builders, substrate-specific enzyme hydrolysis, percarbonate/TAED oxidation and UV-to-visible brightener fluorescence; the latter is not a claim of dirt-mass removal. Wool/protease and colour/bleach limits and fictional product data remain explicit.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-12","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"188bd684-e894-5753-8a50-798220b04d97","goalFingerprint":"sha256:e87f813cff7a6d79e6985fd630f3d60f484542c1e8184d82b14b410bab1db3fe","pageFingerprint":"sha256:c0eb7f94ee62192e9c2b7aab994e554bebcf2c8501a405da351f3af2e2e2bcaf","currentTitleDe":"Farbstoffe als Motor der chemischen Industrie beurteilen","currentTitleEn":"Assess dyes as a driver of the chemical industry","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann die wirtschaftliche Bedeutung der Farbstoffe für die Entwicklung der chemischen Industrie beurteilen.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can assess the economic significance of dyes for the development of the chemical industry.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Industrielle Farbstoffentwicklung verbindet chemische Innovation mit Investition, Anwendungen, Wettbewerb und sozialen Folgen; unterschiedliche Quellen belegen unterschiedliche Ausschnitte.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Industrial dye development connects chemical innovation with investment, applications, competition and social effects; different sources establish different parts of this history.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person beurteilt die wirtschaftliche Bedeutung des synthetischen Indigos anhand tatsächlich zugänglicher historischer Quellen, ordnet Herkunft und Interessen ein und trennt belegte Investition von unbelegtem Gewinn.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner assesses the economic significance of synthetic indigo using actual accessible historical sources, considers provenance and interests and distinguishes documented investment from unproven profit.","transferExpectationDe":"Für den neuen Indanthren-Fall begründet die lernende Person, wie Eigenschaften neue Anwendungen und innerbetrieblichen Wettbewerb ermöglichen, und benennt zusätzliche Belege für eine belastbare langfristige Markt- oder Gewinnbehauptung.","transferExpectationEn":"For the new Indanthrene case, the learner explains how properties enable applications and internal competition and identifies extra evidence needed for a defensible long-term market or profit claim."},"rationale":"Assessing the economic importance of dyes in industrial development is a coherent historical chemistry judgment. It can combine source evidence, interests, uncertainty and tradeoffs without actual laboratory execution or invented quantitative profits. The new actual-source case properly attributes BASF 1897 investment/research figures to company history, separates museum evidence about natural-indigo plantation labour and synthetic displacement, and requires uncertainty rather than fabricated financial returns. The 1901 Indanthrene fresh case does not imply guaranteed permanent market success. However its assessment boundary wrongly requires retained practical execution. P remains REVISE; this D KEEP does not close it.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"revise","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-13","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"5c8f0bbb-103a-579f-87fc-c997afe4fd18","goalFingerprint":"sha256:e083b6eae8abc5d5cbb34b6c9ad3c89024417f321db63204e5d8a3dab1439492","pageFingerprint":"sha256:be8affc9ac6e517e45c7e4141a488e604ba3b7bf3f0e3f482bb2b6d211a7e1cc","currentTitleDe":"Aminocarbonsäuren und Peptide nachweisen","currentTitleEn":"Detect amino carboxylic acids and peptides","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann geeignete Nachweisreaktionen für Aminocarbonsäuren und Peptide durchführen und ihre Aussagekraft etwa bei Lebensmitteln auswerten.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can carry out suitable detection reactions for amino carboxylic acids and peptides and evaluate their evidence, for example in foods.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Nachweisreaktionen sprechen auf geeignete funktionelle Strukturen unter bestimmten Bedingungen an; ein positiver Farbbefund identifiziert eine Stoffklasse nicht immer eindeutig.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Detection reactions respond to suitable functional structures under specified conditions; a positive colour response does not always uniquely identify a substance class.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person wählt geeignete Aminosäure- oder Peptidnachweise, führt die genehmigten Untersuchungen tatsächlich durch, wertet Kontrollen aus und begründet die Grenzen der Farbinterpretation.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner selects suitable amino-acid or peptide tests, actually performs authorized investigations, evaluates controls and explains the limits of colour interpretation.","transferExpectationDe":"Mit vorgegebenen Prolin-, Glycin- und Ethanolaminstrukturen erklärt die lernende Person unterschiedliche Ninhydrinbefunde und ein nicht eindeutiges Positivsignal; dieser Papiertransfer ersetzt die verlangte eigene Durchführung nicht.","transferExpectationEn":"Using supplied proline, glycine and ethanolamine structures, the learner explains different ninhydrin responses and a nonunique positive signal; this paper transfer does not replace required actual execution."},"rationale":"Selecting, actually performing and evaluating appropriate amino-acid/peptide tests is a coherent investigation competence. The current description and prerequisites legitimately retain real practical performance. No remaining P blocker identified. The new proline reference shows secondary ring nitrogen with a carboxyl group and no peptide bond; yellow proline versus purple glycine supports a reagent-specific exception. Supplied ethanolamine is a counterexample to identifying amino acids from a purple response alone. Missing concentrations in an external teaching reference are not turned into a new SOP; paper transfer explicitly does not replace the retained real investigation.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
{"$schema":"https://skillpilot.com/schemas/goal-description-review/v1/goal-description-review-record.schema.json","schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1-14","runId":"chemie-remediation14-independent-a-20261017-observed-science-v1","campaignId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-a","roundId":"chemie-current439-remediation14-author-candidate-20261017-v1-first-pass-a","bundleFingerprint":"sha256:237f4a4840f6c3de63213573b0280df07be4be54a318531d285cb5913e0966af","bookDigest":"sha256:8a7493371017ffb4dae58393923c633e54012fe2cc9f1c3c42621cec2357a3c2","goalId":"64a5bb87-358d-5a22-958a-f66ba5521cd5","goalFingerprint":"sha256:8bcba5cfacd7cb648d6b4d4e82c487893cdc99c5f8e40b34273e45fff4dfad3f","pageFingerprint":"sha256:397cd262fceb8a7eb991db6eff50294d3beac6e05337bd82fc4a8a96947e5a87","currentTitleDe":"Proteinquellen nachhaltig und quellenkritisch bewerten","currentTitleEn":"Evaluate protein sources sustainably and critically","currentDescriptionDe":"Die lernende Person kann tierische und pflanzliche Proteinquellen anhand selbst recherchierter Informationen unter ökologischen, ökonomischen und ethischen Gesichtspunkten vergleichen und die Informationen auf fachliche Richtigkeit, Vertrauenswürdigkeit und Intention prüfen.","currentDescriptionEn":"The learner can compare animal and plant protein sources using independently researched information from ecological, economic and ethical perspectives, and assess the information for scientific accuracy, trustworthiness and intent.","decision":"keep","understandingEvidence":{"essentialUnderstandingDe":"Proteinproduktionswege lassen sich nur mit vergleichbarer Funktion, transparenten Systemgrenzen und geprüften Quellen ökologisch, ökonomisch und ethisch begründet bewerten.","essentialUnderstandingEn":"Protein production routes require a comparable function, transparent system boundaries and checked sources for reasoned ecological, economic and ethical evaluation.","observablePerformanceDe":"Die lernende Person recherchiert selbstständig, dokumentiert die Herkunft der verwendeten Informationen, prüft Gegenquellen und begründet eine begrenzte Bewertung anhand aller drei Kriterienbereiche.","observablePerformanceEn":"The learner independently researches and documents information provenance, checks counter-sources and justifies a bounded evaluation across all three criterion areas.","transferExpectationDe":"Bei einer veränderten Produktionsweise oder widersprüchlichen Daten prüft die lernende Person Vergleichbarkeit und Unsicherheit neu und passt ihr Urteil begründet an, statt pauschal pflanzlich gegen tierisch zu werten.","transferExpectationEn":"For a changed production route or conflicting data, the learner reassesses comparability and uncertainty and justifiably adapts the judgment instead of making a blanket plant-versus-animal ranking."},"rationale":"The explicit independently researched information condition makes an already authentic source-evaluation competence observable. Ecological, economic and ethical comparisons require a common function, source criticism and reasoned judgment rather than an unqualified plant-versus-animal ranking. No remaining P blocker identified. Current tasks require actual learner research provenance, all three criteria, counter-source scrutiny, explicit missing data and a reasoned bounded conclusion. A supplied case is not proof that a learner has already researched; no new recall cards, memory quota or human approval follows.","evidenceProfileContract":"positive-understanding-evidence-v2","evidenceProfileRecommendation":"none","recordStatus":"candidate","reviewAuthority":"ai_candidate"}
